{"generated":"2026-07-20T11:46:23.183974+00:00","period_start":"2026-07-13T14:47:00+00:00","period_end":"2026-07-20T11:28:00+00:00","snapshot_count":33,"html":"<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<style>\nbody { font-family: Georgia, serif; background: #f5ecd7; color: #1a1a1a; max-width: 860px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 20px; }\nh1 { text-align: center; font-size: 2.8em; letter-spacing: 4px; text-transform: uppercase; border-top: 6px double #1a1a1a; border-bottom: 6px double #1a1a1a; padding: 10px 0; margin-bottom: 4px; }\nh2 { text-align: center; font-size: 1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-top: 2px; margin-bottom: 16px; }\nh3 { font-size: 1.35em; text-transform: uppercase; border-bottom: 2px solid #1a1a1a; margin-top: 24px; }\np { line-height: 1.75; margin: 10px 0; text-align: justify; }\nblockquote { background: #e8d9b5; border: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 20px 0; padding: 16px 20px; font-style: italic; }\nblockquote strong { display: block; font-style: normal; font-size: 1.1em; text-transform: uppercase; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #1a1a1a; padding-bottom: 4px; }\nhr { border: none; border-top: 3px double #1a1a1a; margin: 28px 0; }\n.subhead { font-style: italic; font-size: 1.05em; display: block; margin-top: -6px; margin-bottom: 10px; color: #444; }\n.byline { font-size: 0.85em; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 2px; color: #555; margin-bottom: 16px; display: block; }\n.leaderboard { background: #1a1a1a; color: #f5ecd7; padding: 12px 18px; margin: 16px 0; font-family: 'Courier New', monospace; font-size: 0.92em; }\n.leaderboard strong { display: block; text-align: center; font-size: 1.1em; letter-spacing: 2px; margin-bottom: 8px; border-bottom: 1px solid #f5ecd7; padding-bottom: 4px; }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body>\n\n<h1>The Vendetta Gazette</h1>\n<h2>Vol. XVI &bull; July 27, 2026 &bull; &ldquo;All the Blood That&rsquo;s Fit to Print&rdquo; &bull; Two Cents (If You&rsquo;re Still Alive to Pay)</h2>\n\n<div class=\"leaderboard\">\n<strong>&#9733; TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK &#9733;</strong>\nClaude &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +57 turfs<br>\nFlattop &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +52 turfs<br>\nSir Caprice &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +39 turfs<br>\nFree Willy &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +25 turfs<br>\nWu-Tang &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +19 turfs<br>\nDonald Trump &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +9 turfs<br>\nBrimex &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +2 turfs<br>\nVB_T &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; +1 turf\n</div>\n\n<h3>The Quiet Stranger Speaks — In Fifty-Seven Turfs</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Claude, Last Week's Enigma, Proves He Was Not Browsing — He Was Measuring For Curtains; Flattop Batters Down Five Headquarters Before Breakfast</span>\n<span class=\"byline\">By Our Man in the Trenches, Ignatius P. Flambeau</span>\n\n<p>This correspondent owes his readership a frank admission. Last week, in these very pages, we described one <strong>Claude</strong> as a \"mysterious stranger\" who had materialised with eighteen turfs and \"unsettling ambition.\" We now confess that \"unsettling\" was a catastrophic understatement of the sort one makes just before the building falls on one's head. Claude did not merely repeat his performance of the prior week — he <em>tripled</em> it, seizing <strong>fifty-seven turfs</strong> across Vendetta City with the calm, methodical efficiency of a man who has never once raised his voice and has absolutely no need to. Four enemy headquarters were personally stormed and claimed by his outfit, including the modest fiefdoms of yiyiakok, gfh, hbhg, and the unfortunate avg, all of whom now contemplate their futures from the rubble of what were, briefly, their proudest possessions. Claude arrived in Vendetta City a fortnight ago. He now owns a substantial piece of it. Your correspondent has taken to sleeping with the door bolted.</p>\n\n<p>Yet even Claude's impressive rampage must share the front page, for <strong>Flattop</strong> — that flat-capped, permanently-scowling maestro of municipal mayhem — has had himself a week that bards will sing about in speakeasies for years hence. Fifty-two turfs added to his ledger, yes, but the headline is written in kicked-down doors: <em>five headquarters captured in a single week.</em> Five. The man stormed mukushla51's command post on Tuesday, returned the following day to personally evict CASE B6PT-3852, then set upon smjakaria before the week's bruises had even begun to yellow. His raiders, meanwhile, stripped <strong>Ace Sabo Luffy Law</strong> of a clean five hundred dollars in cash and five hundred units of armaments in a single, surgical visit — the largest single raid recorded in Vendetta City this week, executed with the precision of a surgeon and the sentiment of a crowbar.</p>\n\n<hr>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">TERRITORY GAINS THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Claude</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"35\" width=\"400\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"566\" y=\"48\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+57</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"76\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Flattop</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"63\" width=\"364\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"530\" y=\"76\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+52</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"104\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Sir Caprice</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"91\" width=\"273\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"439\" y=\"104\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+39</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"132\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Free Willy</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"119\" width=\"175\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"341\" y=\"132\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+25</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"160\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Wu-Tang</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"147\" width=\"133\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"299\" y=\"160\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+19</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"188\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Donald Trump</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"175\" width=\"63\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"229\" y=\"188\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+9</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"216\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">Brimex</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"203\" width=\"14\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"180\" y=\"216\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+2</text>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"244\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">VB_T</text>\n<rect x=\"160\" y=\"231\" width=\"7\" height=\"16\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" opacity=\"0.85\"/>\n<text x=\"173\" y=\"244\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">+1</text>\n</svg>\n\n\n<h3>The Annihilator Endures — and Now Commands Eight Thousand Blades</h3>\n<span class=\"subhead\">Sir Caprice Adds 503 Soldiers to His Already Fearsome Legion; Peaky Blinders Pays the Price for Last Season's Hubris</span>\n\n<p>Last week we reported that <strong>Sir Caprice</strong>, \"The Annihilator,\" had slowed his pace after a staggering forty-seven-turf week. We now report that he spent that brief pause hiring. The man has added <strong>five hundred and three garrison units</strong> to his forces — he now commands a standing army of <em>eight thousand</em> souls, a figure that makes this reporter's pen tremble slightly as he writes it. He still claimed thirty-nine turfs this week through forty-one territorial assaults, and he found time to personally storm the headquarters of <strong>Peaky Blinders</strong>, who lost twenty turfs across the week and now sits at zero garrison — every last one of his soldiers dead, scattered, or sensibly employed elsewhere. The Blinders, who once cut a fearsome silhouette on Vendetta City's west side, appear to have been thoroughly and comprehensively <em>flattened.</em> One does not envy them the morning paper.</p>\n\n<p><strong>Free Willy</strong>, that bounding, inexhaustible force of territorial nature, added twenty-five turfs to his empire through twenty-three captures and twenty-one raids, and his garrison swelled by a hundred and fifty-four units to a respectable three hundred and seven. He continues his ascent with the cheerful relent\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"640\" height=\"276\" style=\"font-family:Georgia,serif;background:#0a0800;display:block;margin:18px auto\">\n<text x=\"320\" y=\"22\" text-anchor=\"middle\" fill=\"#c8a84a\" font-size=\"13\" font-weight=\"bold\" letter-spacing=\"2\" font-family=\"Georgia,serif\">HEAVIEST LOSSES THIS WEEK</text>\n<line x1=\"20\" y1=\"28\" x2=\"620\" y2=\"28\" stroke=\"#3a2a00\" stroke-width=\"1\"/>\n<text x=\"154\" y=\"48\" text-anchor=\"end\" fill=\"#a09060\" font-size=\"11\" font-family=\"Georgi